    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="1113" n="1099" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1099"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/7–1944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-19T22:00:00+01:00">July 19, 1944—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [ReceivedJuly 19—12:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4604. Your 1945, June 6; my 4260, July 5.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d647-f1"/>
                    Foreign Office note dated yesterday states according telegram from Swiss
                    Legation, Budapest, Hungarian Government has authorized departure from Hungary
                    all Jews in possession entry permit for another country, including
                        Palestine.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d647-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>According same message German Government will permit transit through occupied
                    territories. Necessary measures for evacuation will <pb facs="1114" n="1100"
                        xml:id="pg1100"/> be taken soon as possible by Swiss Legation in
                    collaboration with Palestinian Bureau, Budapest. Travel documents will probably
                    be Hungarian police passports.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d647-f1" n="24" xml:id="d647-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d647-f2" n="25" xml:id="d647-f2-content">
                <p>For original statement on Hungarian offer made public in Switzerland by the
                    Intercross on July 18, see circular telegram of August 18, <ref target="#pg1127"
                        >p. 1127</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
